course: dictionary
lesson: 7352
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word play is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» Here playing means doing something fun, because that is what makes time feel short.
explain: «His dad plays a fighting game with him on Sunday mornings, sitting right next to him.» Here plays means takes part in a game. The clues are game and sitting next to him. Always ask: does my meaning fit in the sentence?
explain: Play can also be a noun, a thing you can watch. A play is a story acted out on a stage. If you see «a play» with a or the in front of it, it is usually a show, not a game. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Play can be a verb (a doing word) or a noun (a naming word).
fact: The verb forms are play, plays, played and playing.
fact: «Play» can mean doing something for fun, like a game or a sport.
fact: «Play» can mean making music with an instrument, or turning it on. «Play a part» means acting as a character in a show.
fact: «Play» can also mean time spent having fun. LEGO's name comes from the Danish "leg godt", which means "play well".
exercise: «His dad plays a fighting game with him on Sunday mornings.» What does plays mean here? | Acts as a character in a show | Turns on a radio | *Takes part in a game for fun | Waits quietly for a bus
exercise: «Time feels shorter when you are playing and longer when you are waiting.» What does playing mean here? | *Doing something fun, like a game | Reading a long book | Sleeping in bed | Going shopping
exercise: «Our class will put on a play next week.» What is a play here? | *A story acted out on a stage | A quiet time at school | A kind of game with a ball | Something to eat at lunch
test: «The band will play a song for us.» What does play mean here? | To sleep in | To go to a shop | *To make music with an instrument | To run a race
test: «She played the part of the wicked witch.» What does played the part mean? | To paint a picture | To cook dinner for everyone | *To act as a character in a show | To run fast in a race
exam: «Our class will put on a play next week.» What does play mean in this sentence? | *A story acted out on a stage | Time spent having fun | To make music | A pet bird
